# Build-context exclusions for this Dockerfile (BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore in
# preference to .dockerignore, so this file is used whatever .dockerignore a host keeps locally).
#
# The Dockerfile copies the whole context (`COPY . .`). Without these rules, a build from a
# working checkout bakes the deployment's secrets and data into the image layers.
# Gate: test/test_dockerignore.py (every secret below is excluded; nothing the image needs is).

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
*.env
!.env.example
tda_keys/jwt_secret.key
tda_keys/provenance_key.pem
tda_keys/provenance_key.pub
tda_keys/license.local.key
tda_keys/license.local.key.previous
tda_keys/test_*.pem
deploy/mcp/*/.env
maintenance/licensing/

# ── Per-deployment data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tda_auth.db
tda_auth.db-*
tda_auth.db.bak-*
tda_eval.db
tda_eval.db-*
tda_eval/
tda_sessions/
tda_files/
tda_skills/
rag/
backups/
marketplace_data/
prompt_overrides/
.chromadb_rag_cache/
chroma_db/
tda_chroma_db/
logs/
*.log
agent_packs/*/corpus/
agent_packs/*/import_output/
agent_packs/*/pipeline_config.json

# ── Not part of the server ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Benchmark harnesses run beside a deployment, never inside it. docs/ stays: the knowledge
# sync reads file:// sources relative to the project root (core/knowledge_sync.py).
benchmarks/

# ── Build and editor noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
venv/
env/
.venv/
node_modules/
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.claude/settings.local.json
.gemini/
*.tmp
*.bak
.DS_Store
